From f23254ddd67d7c2393ba85c2395464ec433491e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Revitt <max@revitt.co>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 10:28:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(pgstorage): disambiguate already-claimed check by
 source rollup

GetPendingDepositsToClaim (count + rows) and GetDepositsFromOtherL2ToClaim
excluded a deposit whenever any sync.claim row shared (network_id, index),
ignoring the claim's origin (rollup_index / mainnet_flag).

On a shared AggLayer rollup manager every rollup claims its L2->L1 exits on
L1 under network_id=0, and their deposit_cnt index spaces overlap. So once
any rollup claimed its exit #N, every other rollup's exit #N was permanently
hidden from /pending-bridges and the standalone auto-claimer never submitted
it (logging "No bridges to claim were found"). /bridges reported them
claimable the whole time because GetClaim already uses the strict
rollup_index + 1 = network_id key.

Mirror GetClaim's origin key in all three pending-deposit checks:

  (d.network_id = 0  AND c.mainnet_flag)
  OR (d.network_id <> 0 AND NOT c.mainnet_flag AND c.rollup_index + 1 = d.network_id)

No schema/migration change; single-rollup deployments are unaffected.

Adds TestGetPendingDepositsToClaimCrossRollup, which reproduces the
collision (rollup 76 exits 13/14/23 while rollups 44/49/52/57 have claimed
their own #23): fails on the unqualified query (0 deposits) and passes with
the fix (3 deposits, then 2 once rollup 76 claims its own #23).
